    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Corbin Carroll**, whose 83.53 efficiency score makes him our premier start. Facing a favorable matchup against G. Holmes, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from elite volume in the #2 hole and a matchup that leverages his primary weapon: speed. While Holmes holds a 4.65 xERA, the dynamic platoon advantage and a projected boost from the base scoring indicate he is poised to anchor our production today. Alongside him, **Josh Naylor** provides significant muscle in the middle of the order; his 73.37 score is heavily supported by a high SP skill advantage against Wesneski, making him our most reliable bet for RBI contributions. **Mickey Moniak** also warrants attention, as his 68.92 score is bolstered by a rare wind-out scenario and an advantageous #3 spot, pushing his output well above the marginal threshold.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jose Caballero** on the pine. Despite his profile as a high-upside speed threat, the optimizer was forced to bench him due to his absence from today\u2019s official lineup and a sub-optimal platoon split against Fisher. He represents the clearest \"next man up\" should we need a defensive replacement or a late-game pivot for stolen bases. Meanwhile, we remain cautious regarding **Travis Bazzana**; his 42.21 score is hovering near the floor. While the SP skill advantage is present, the L/L platoon disadvantage and the bottom-third order placement make him a candidate for an early hook if he doesn't find rhythm against Peralta. With **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** currently sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the consistency of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Seiya Suzuki** to maintain our efficiency metrics as we navigate a high-volume slate.",
